[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Do I need to install this?[/b][/size][/color]
Only if a mod you want tells you to. NCZoningCore is a shared dependency, like Codeware or RED4ext: it sits in the background and provides data to the mods that ask for it.

[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]What it does under the hood[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*]Downloads the registry once per game session over HTTPS.
[*]Caches it on disk, so it works offline after the first online launch and revalidates efficiently (no re-download when nothing changed).
[*]Serves the data to redscript and CET Lua mods through a small, stable API.
[/list]
It makes [b]no[/b] changes to your game: no writes, no telemetry, no position tracking, no UI.
[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*]RED4ext
[*]redscript
[*]Codeware
[*]RedData
[*]RedFileSystem
[*]RedHttpClient
[/list]
[i]Cyber Engine Tweaks is [b]not[/b] required by NCZoningCore itself. It is only needed if the consumer mod using NCZoningCore is a CET Lua mod.[/i]
[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size][/color]
[list=1]
[*]Install the requirements above.
[*]Download NCZoningCore and extract the [font=Courier New]r6[/font] folder into your Cyberpunk 2077 root directory.
[i]Final path should look like:[/i] [font=Courier New]Cyberpunk 2077\r6\scripts\NCZoningCore\[/font]
[/list]
Works with mod managers, or install manually.
[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]For mod authors[/b][/size][/color]
Build on NCZoningCore from redscript or CET Lua. The full consumer guide and worked examples for both are in the GitHub repository linked on this page.

In short: redscript consumers [font=Courier New]import NCZoning.Api.*[/font] (or guard with [font=Courier New]@if(ModuleExists("NCZoning.Api"))[/font] for a soft dependency) and subscribe to the [font=Courier New]NCZoning-DataReady[/font] / [font=Courier New]-DataRefreshed[/font] / [font=Courier New]-DataError[/font] events. CET Lua consumers call the [font=Courier New]NCZoningApi[/font] facade and observe [font=Courier New]NCZoningApi.OnDataReady[/font] for the data-ready signal.
[line]
[color=#ffff00][size=5][b]A note on game updates[/b][/size][/color]
NCZoningCore is pure redscript and survives game patches on its own, but its plugin requirements (Codeware and the Red* plugins) usually need a rebuild by their authors after each Cyberpunk update. Right after a game update the framework can be temporarily unavailable until those catch up. Mods that depend on it with a soft dependency keep working in that window.
[line]
